#
# Technology-independent synthesis down to Yosys' internal gate library
# ($_AND_, $_OR_, $_MUX_, $_DFF_*, ...). Expects the design to be read and
# `hierarchy -top` to have been run already (see the `synth` Makefile target).
#
# Inferred memories are kept as generic $mem_v2 cells instead of being
# expanded into flip-flops: the 64 MiB shared RAM and the 256 KiB scratchpads
# are far too large for that, and they stand in for SRAM macros anyway.

# Coarse-grain synthesis (proc, fsm, alumacc, share, memory -nomap, ...).
synth -run begin:fine

# Fine-grain synthesis as in `synth`, minus memory_map.
opt -fast -full
opt -full
techmap
opt -fast
abc
opt -fast

hierarchy -check
check
